  "ManualPage": {
    "title": "User Manual",
    "subtitle": "Master AgriKoutaba for your Cameroonian agribusiness.",
    "introTitle": "Getting Started",
    "introContent": "AgriKoutaba is designed to digitize the traditional 'paper and pencil' records of Cameroonian farms. By centralizing your operations, you gain real-time insights into your financial health and production efficiency.",
    "productionTitle": "Production & Cycles",
    "productionContent": "The core of the system. First, register your 'Plots' in the Production section. Once a plot is registered, you can start a 'Crop Cycle' (e.g., Maize, Cocoa). When the crop is ready, record a 'Harvest' to automatically calculate your profit and log sales income.",
    "laborTitle": "Labor & Wages",
    "laborContent": "In the 'Crop Cycles' tab, use the menu (three dots) to assign workers to a cycle. When you record a wage, the system automatically creates a financial Expense. This ensures your production costs are accurate.",
    "financeTitle": "Financial Management",
    "financeContent": "All transactions are tracked in FCFA. The Finances page allows you to log every income and expense. The Dashboard provides a visual overview of your net income, helping you make data-driven decisions.",
    "rolesTitle": "Roles & Security",
    "rolesContent": "To ensure data integrity, AgriKoutaba uses three roles: Admin (Full control), Manager (Can edit data), and Worker (View-only). The owner email (mbongmebiang@gmail.com) is always an Admin.",
    "moreInfo": "For more assistance, please contact support."
  },
